{"name":"Breathless","hex":"#dfdae0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"breathless","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having difficulty breathing; gasping.","That makes one hold one's breath (with excitement etc.)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breathless"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breathless (1960 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Breathless is a 1960 French New Wave crime drama film written and directed by Jean-Luc Godard. It stars Jean-Paul Belmondo as a wandering criminal named Michel, and Jean Seberg as his American girlfriend Patricia. The film was Godard's first feature-length work and represented Belmondo's breakthrough as an actor."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3f/%C3%80_bout_de_souffle_%28movie_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breathless_(1960_film)","wikidata":"Q86427"},{"title":"Breathless (1983 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Breathless is a 1983 American neo-noir romantic thriller film directed by Jim McBride, written by McBride and L. M. Kit Carson, and starring Richard Gere and Valérie Kaprisky. It is a remake of the 1960 French film of the same name directed by Jean-Luc Godard and written by Godard and François Truffaut. The original film is about an American woman and a French criminal in Paris, while the remake is vice versa in Los Angeles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/28/Breathless_%281983%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breathless_(1983_film)","wikidata":"Q754304"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2d/Breathless-Screenshot-01.jpg/330px-Breathless-Screenshot-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2d/Breathless-Screenshot-01.jpg/330px-Brea